{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Bw8ZfBm7265EXGRtgFGqfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我先检查当前 experiment_plan 中所有 status 为 planned 或 RUNNING 的实验，以及 what_if 条目，然后逐一在 worst 档下展开预测。\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe: 从 \"scale-robust depth estimation framework\" 转向 \"characterizing the scale boundary of recursive depth signals\"。\n  14B 实验彻底失败（4-class acc <55%，feature pattern 与 1B 矛盾），theory section 无法解释 scale failure，\n  existing detectors 在 shallow depth 与我们性能接近。论文仍冲 EMNLP Main，但从 framework paper 变为\n  characterization + negative result paper。新 story spine: depth signal 在 ≤1.5B 强且系统性，\n  但在 14B 戏剧性衰减——scale boundary 本身是 finding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: 13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"14B clean FP16 scale validation — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3 递归链, 19 特征提取, RF/LR 分类。\n      验证 depth signal 在 14B 是否持续。\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.42\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.405, 0.435]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.38\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.37\n      auc_d0v1: 0.78\n      auc_d1v2: 0.53\n      auc_d1v3: 0.62\n      auc_d2v3: 0.52\n      edd_at_075: 1\n      top_features:\n        - p25_ppl\n        - type_token_ratio\n        - mean_ppl\n        - rep_3gram\n        - surprisal_std\n      top2_feature_overlap_with_1b: 0\n      finetune_losses:\n        depth_0: 1.85\n        depth_1: 1.72\n        depth_2: 1.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B 模型容量远大于训练数据复杂度，LoRA fine-tune 后模型快速逼近 attractor distribution，\n      depth-1 与 depth-2/3 的输出分布差异被大模型的 capacity headroom 吸收。具体机制：\n      (1) 14B 的 residual stream 维度（5120 vs 1B 的 2048）使得 LoRA rank-16 的参数扰动\n      相对于总参数量极小（<0.02%），fine-tune 后模型行为变化微弱，递归链各 depth 输出高度相似；\n      (2) finetune loss 从 d0=1.85 到 d2=1.68 仅下降 0.17（1B 模型下降 >1.0），说明\n      14B 在 depth-0 已经 well-fit 数据，后续 depth fine-tune 几乎无额外压缩——\n      Shumailov tail erosion 发生在 depth-0→1 就已完成；\n      (3) d0v1 AUC=0.78 尚可但远低于 1B 的 0.99+，说明即便 real vs gen-1 的区分也大幅退化；\n      (4) top features 完全改变——1B 中 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 是 dominant pair，\n      14B 中这两个特征的跨 depth 方差坍缩，排名退出 top-5，取而代之的是 lexical diversity\n      和低分位 perplexity 特征，这些在 1B 中 importance <0.03；\n      (5) EDD=1（仅 d0v1 AUC>0.75），与 1B 的 EDD=4 严重不一致——\"scale robustness\" claim 不可维持。\n      总结：14B 的 depth signal collapse 是 genuine phenomenon，不是方法缺陷，\n      因为 finetune loss pattern 本身就显示 distribution 在 14B scale 没有足够分化。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 14B vs 1-1.5B comparison — 4-class acc, EDD, top-2 feature overlap\"\n      - \"Table: 14B pairwise AUC matrix (d0v1 through d2v3)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve: 14B (flat near 0.5 for d1v2/d2v3) vs 1B models (monotonic decay from ~0.95)\"\n      - \"Feature importance bar chart: 14B top-10 vs 1B consensus top-10, showing zero overlap in top-2\"\n    analysis: >\n      14B 4-class acc=42% 仅略高于 chance (25%)，且 feature pattern 与 1B 完全矛盾。\n      这构成 worst tier 核心假设的直接确认。论文必须 reframe：depth signal 存在 scale boundary，\n      1-1.5B 内信号强且一致，14B 处信号坍缩。Finetune loss 的 shallow gradient \n      (1.85→1.68 across 3 depths) 提供了机制解释：大模型一次 fine-tune 就到达 attractor 附近，\n      后续 depth 无法产生可区分的 distributional shift。这与 Dohmatob 的 contraction rate 理论\n      一致（capacity 越大，contraction 越快），但 Theory section 的定量 bound 与实际 EDD 不匹配。\n      与 Instruct 实验 (47.4%) 和 base 7B (60%) 共同构成一致 pattern：方法仅对 ≤1.5B base 模型\n      fully effective。必须在 paper 中将此作为 \"scale boundary characterization\" finding，\n      而非 failure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: Wild-data calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      从 C4/FineWeb/RedPajama 抽取子集，用 trained RF 分类器做 depth 预测 + 分布分析，\n      验证 depth signal 在野生数据中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      c4_d0_pct: 62.0\n      c4_fpr: 38.0\n      fineweb_d0_pct: 68.0\n      fineweb_fpr: 32.0\n      redpajama_d0_pct: 60.0\n      redpajama_fpr: 40.0\n      cross_model_consistency_jaccard: 0.35\n      wikitext_d0_pct: 95.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下，wild-data FPR 高达 30-40%，远超此前单数据集实验 (C4 20%, FineWeb 19%)。\n      原因：(1) RedPajama 包含大量 Common Crawl 低质量文本（ads, boilerplate, auto-generated content），\n      这些文本的 repetition + low diversity 特征与 depth-1+ 递归文本高度重叠——\n      RF 的 decision boundary 无法区分 \"genuinely recursive\" 与 \"naturally repetitive\"；\n      (2) 多数据集扩展暴露了之前 OpenWebText (FPR 0.9-2.8%) 是 best case 的事实——\n      editorial-quality web data 很少，raw crawl 的 FPR 才是 realistic deployment scenario；\n      (3) cross-model consistency Jaccard=0.35 远低于此前 controlled 实验的 0.667，\n      说明不同 reference model 对 wild data 的 depth assignment 不一致——\n      在 controlled 设置中 reference model 差异被共享的递归 pattern 掩盖，\n      wild data 中 domain shift 放大了 reference model 偏差；\n      (4) WikiText 仍有 5% FPR（此前 0-1.5%），因为 RedPajama-calibrated RF \n      的 decision boundary shift 导致部分 formulaic academic writing 被误判。\n      结论：depth estimator 在 wild data 的 false positive rate 太高，\n      实际部署需要 domain-specific calibration，这严重限制了 practical claim。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: FPR comparison across 5 datasets (WikiText/C4/FineWeb/OpenWebText/RedPajama)\"\n      - \"Table: Cross-model consistency (3 reference models × 3 datasets)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: FPR by dataset, showing editorial (low) vs crawl (high) pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      FPR 30-40% on raw crawl 意味着 depth estimator 不能 out-of-the-box 部署到 web-scale curation。\n      但 consistent pattern (editorial低/crawl高) 本身是有价值的 finding，\n      说明 FPR 可预测且与 content quality 相关。Paper 必须 honest scope：\n      depth estimation 对 curated corpora 可靠，对 raw crawl 需要额外 domain calibration。\n      这与 worst tier 叙事一致：方法有 clear boundary conditions。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: Existing detector ordinal baseline\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Existing detector ordinal baseline — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT 连续分数校准为 ordinal bin，在 3×3 已有数据上评估\n      ordinal depth estimation 能力。\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc: 0.58\n      binoculars_3class_acc: 0.52\n      binoculars_d0v1_auc: 0.98\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.62\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc: 0.62\n      fastdetectgpt_3class_acc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_d0v1_auc: 0.97\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.58\n      rf_4class_acc_ref: 0.78\n      delta_rf_vs_best_detector: 0.16\n      detector_shallow_acc_d0d1d2: 0.65\n      rf_shallow_acc_d0d1d2: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档假设 existing detectors 达到 50-65% ordinal acc，这里 Binoculars=58%, \n      Fast-DetectGPT=62%。关键在 shallow depth 的竞争：\n      (1) 两个 detector 在 d0v1 AUC ≈0.97-0.98，与我们的 0.99 几乎相同——\n      real vs gen-1 区分上 existing detectors 本身就足够好，\n      因为它们本来就是为 binary detection 设计的；\n      (2) d1v2 AUC 达到 0.62-0.68，与我们在 topk50 cell 的性能 (0.75-0.83) 有差距\n      但不是 dramatic——特别是 Fast-DetectGPT 的 0.68 与 Pythia topk50 的 0.75 只差 7pp；\n      (3) d2v3 是我们真正拉开差距的地方 (0.55-0.58 vs 我们的 0.69-0.88)，\n      但 reviewer 会指出 deep depth 区分在 practical curation 中 marginal value 有限；\n      (4) 特别危险的是：如果 reviewer 做 binary \"shallow(d0-d1) vs deep(d2-d3)\" simplification，\n      detectors 的表现会更接近我们——因为 coarser granularity 下 existing scores 足够。\n      本质原因：Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT 的 scoring function 隐含 captures depth-related\n      distributional shift 的某些方面（尤其是 tail behavior），虽然不是 ordinal-aware 的，\n      但 calibrated regression 可以利用 score 的 monotonic trend。\n      我们的优势集中在 (a) ordinal structure awareness, (b) d2+ depth pairs，\n      但如果这些 depth 在 14B 消失了，优势领域的 practical relevance 受质疑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT — per-pair AUC comparison\"\n      - \"Table: Simplified binary (shallow/deep) accuracy comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: pairwise AUC by method, showing convergence at shallow depths and divergence at deep\"\n    analysis: >\n      Existing detectors 在 ordinal task 上表现好于 expected (尤其 Fast-DetectGPT 62%)，\n      在 shallow depth (d0/d1) 与 RF 性能接近。我们的 clear advantage 仅在 d2v3 pair。\n      这不致命——我们仍有 16pp advantage overall，且 ordinal structure 是 novel contribution——\n      但 reviewer 可能认为 marginal improvement 不 justify task formalization overhead。\n      Paper 必须强调：(a) detector 的 ordinal acc 是 post-hoc calibration 非 native 能力，\n      (b) 我们提供 interpretable feature analysis (Atlas) 而非 black-box score，\n      (c) cross-strategy robustness 是 detectors 未被测试的。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Table 1 bootstrap CIs\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Table 1 bootstrap CIs — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      从已有 5-fold CV 结果计算 bootstrap confidence intervals for all 9 cells。\n      纯分析任务。\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_pp: 3.2\n      max_ci_width_pp: 5.1\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.671, 0.722]\n      pythia_topk50_ci_width: 5.1\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.838, 0.872]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci_width: 3.4\n      cells_with_ci_width_gt_4pp: 3\n      overlap_between_worst_and_best_cell: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI 宽度取决于 fold variance。Worst 档下，部分 cells（尤其 topk50 cells）\n      的 fold-to-fold variance 较大，导致 CI 宽度达 5pp+。\n      (1) Pythia topk50 是 worst cell (69.6%)，其 fold variance 本身就高（5-fold range ~4pp），\n      bootstrap 放大后 CI 可达 [0.671, 0.722]——下限接近 chance×2.7，不够 impressive；\n      (2) 更关键的是 CI overlap：如果 pythia_topk50 上限 (72.2%) 与 chance baseline \n      的 bootstrap 上限 (28-30%) 还有 gap 没问题，但与 LR baseline (68.2%) 的 CI 重叠——\n      说明在 weakest cell 中 RF vs LR 优势不 statistically significant；\n      (3) 三个 topk50 cells 的 CI width 都 >4pp，说明 topk50 strategy 下 \n      depth signal 本身 noisy，不只是分类器问题；\n      (4) 好消息是 best cells (GPT-2 XL temp09/nucleus) CI tight (3.4pp)，\n      但 reviewer 会 focus on worst cells。\n      本质原因：topk50 的 k=50 truncation 保留了足够 token diversity 使 depth signal 弱于 \n      nucleus (尾部截断更激进→更 distinctive) 和 temp09 (全 logit 放缩→更 distinctive)。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1 (revised): 3×3 matrix with bootstrap 95% CIs\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CI 本身不改变 point estimates，但 worst 档的风险在于 reviewer 关注 CI overlap。\n      如果 weakest cells 的 RF vs simple baseline CI 重叠，\n      reviewer 可能降低对 \"consistent feature-based advantage\" claim 的信心。\n      Mitigation: report CI transparently，强调 9/9 cells 均 >chance (25%) 的 consistency，\n      而非 individual cell significance。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Theoretical analysis (Theory section)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Theoretical analysis — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      连接 depth signal 到 model collapse theory: (1) tail erosion 机制解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal，\n      (2) EDD 上界推导基于 contraction rate，(3) 与实验 EDD 对照验证。\n    expected_results:\n      theory_edd_upper_bound: 3\n      empirical_edd_1b: 4\n      theory_vs_empirical_error: 1\n      theory_edd_bound_14b: 2\n      empirical_edd_14b: 1\n      theory_vs_empirical_error_14b: 1\n      contraction_rate_bound_tight: false\n      tail_erosion_qualitative_match: true\n      tail_erosion_quantitative_match: false\n      strategy_convergence_rate_explanation: \"qualitative only, no closed-form\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 Theory section 的核心问题：无法定量解释 14B failure。\n      (1) Tail erosion 机制（Shumailov et al.）在 1B scale 定性匹配——\n      p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 作为 tail statistics 确实随 depth 单调衰减，\n      与 \"recursive generation erodes tail of learned distribution\" 一致——\n      但定量上，Shumailov 的 Gaussian approximation 预测 tail 衰减速率 \n      与实际 perplexity distribution (heavy-tailed, non-Gaussian) 不匹配：\n      predicted variance contraction ~0.7x per depth vs actual ~0.85x；\n      (2) EDD 上界推导依赖 Dohmatob 的 contraction rate theorem，\n      但该 theorem 假设 distribution family closure (Gaussian → Gaussian)，\n      而实际 LM output distribution 非 Gaussian——推导的 EDD bound=3 < empirical EDD=4，\n      bound 不 tight 且方向错（应是 upper bound，结果低于实际）；\n      (3) 对 14B，理论预测 EDD=2（更快 contraction due to larger capacity），\n      但实际 EDD=1——差距虽然 \"方向一致\" 但具体数值不匹配，\n      且 Theory 无法解释为什么 14B 的 feature pattern 与 1B 完全不同\n      （理论只预测 \"signal weaker\"，不预测 \"feature ranking changes\"）；\n      (4) Strategy-dependent convergence rate（temp09 reversal）只能做 qualitative argument\n      （\"uniform scaling accelerates convergence\"），无 closed-form expression，\n      reviewer 会认为这是 hand-waving；\n      (5) 最致命的是 14B failure + theory mismatch 的组合：\n      如果 theory 能精确预测 \"14B should fail\"，那 negative result 有 explanatory value；\n      但 theory 预测 EDD=2 而实际 EDD=1，说明 theory 连 negative result 也没完全解释。\n      结论：Theory section 从 \"grounding contribution\" 降级为 \"suggestive framework with acknowledged gaps\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Theoretical EDD bound vs empirical EDD across scales (1B, 7B, 14B)\"\n      - \"Table: Predicted vs actual contraction rates by model scale\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contraction rate curve: theoretical prediction vs empirical measurement, showing gap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section 在 worst 档不能作为 independent contribution，\n      只能作为 \"partial explanation\" 放在 Discussion。\n      理论与实验的不一致（EDD bound error ≥1 across scales）\n      使得 \"theoretical grounding\" 这条 sell point 基本失效。\n      Reviewer 可能评论 \"the theoretical analysis is hand-wavy and does not add to the empirical findings\"。\n      Mitigation: 诚实报告 theory 的 limitations，将 theory-empirical gap 本身作为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_026: API model recursive chains\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"API model recursive chains — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归链 + prompted recursive chain，\n      验证 depth signal 在商用模型中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4omini_ft_4class_acc: 0.38\n      gpt4omini_ft_d1v2_auc: 0.52\n      gpt4omini_prompted_4class_acc: 0.30\n      gpt4omini_prompted_d1v2_auc: 0.51\n      api_cost_usd: 120\n      feature_overlap_with_1b: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 API 模型结果与 14B failure 一致且更极端。\n      (1) GPT-4o-mini 是 distilled large model，其 capacity 远超 1.5B——\n      与 14B 相同的 mechanism (capacity headroom 吸收 recursive perturbation) 适用，\n      且更严重因为 RLHF/DPO alignment 进一步 regularize output distribution，\n      使得不同 depth 的输出更加 homogeneous；\n      (2) Fine-tuning API 限制 (3 epochs max, no LoRA control, black-box optimizer) \n      意味着 fine-tune 幅度可能不足以产生 measurable distributional shift——\n      API model 的 safety guardrails 可能 cap 了 distribution drift；\n      (3) Prompted chain (rewrite/continue without fine-tune) 更糟——\n      大模型的 instruction following 能力使其 \"rewrite\" 时保持 style consistency，\n      depth-1 rewrite 与 depth-0 original 在 statistical features 上几乎不可区分；\n      (4) Feature ranking 完全改变，因为 API model 的 tokenizer 和 vocabulary 不同，\n      且 reference model (Pythia) 与 target model (GPT-4o-mini) 的 distribution mismatch\n      可能主导 feature values，掩盖 genuine depth signal；\n      (5) $120 cost for negative result 是 acceptable 但 reviewer 可能问 \n      \"why not test more API models\" —— 在 worst 档下 one negative 就够了。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: API model depth estimation vs local model comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      API model failure 在 worst 档下是 expected，与 14B failure + instruct failure (47.4%)\n      构成完整 pattern：depth signal 仅在 small base models 中存在。\n      这强化了 \"scale boundary\" 叙事但进一步 narrow 了方法 applicability。\n      Paper 可以 frame 为：\"depth estimation is a small-model phenomenon, \n      which is still practically relevant because small models generate \n      a disproportionate share of recursive web content\"——但这个 argument 的 reviewer \n      acceptability 取决于是否能找到 convincing citation for small model prevalence in web crawl。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # what_if: theory_section\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Theory section (what_if) — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: >\n      Half-page theoretical sketch: tail erosion mechanism, EDD upper bound,\n      strategy convergence rate. 验证与实验数据 consistency。\n    expected_results:\n      tail_erosion_qualitative_fit: true\n      tail_erosion_quantitative_fit: false\n      edd_bound_derivation: \"EDD ≤ floor(log(1/ε) / log(1/λ)) where λ is contraction rate\"\n      edd_bound_1b_predicted: 3\n      edd_bound_1b_actual: 4\n      edd_bound_14b_predicted: 2\n      edd_bound_14b_actual: 1\n      bound_direction: \"consistently underestimates empirical EDD at 1B, overestimates at 14B\"\n      strategy_convergence_closed_form: false\n      reviewer_assessment: \"interesting but not rigorous enough for a theory contribution\"\n      simulated_meta_score_impact: +0.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 plan_023 预测一致。Theory section 的 worst 档特征是 \"directionally correct, \n      quantitatively wrong\"：\n      (1) Tail erosion 定性正确——recursive generation 确实 erodes distribution tails，\n      这与 p90_ppl 的 diagnostic power 一致——但 Shumailov 的 formalism \n      假设 continuous density estimation，而 LM 是 discrete token-level distribution，\n      mapping 不 exact；\n      (2) EDD bound formula 看起来 elegant 但依赖 contraction rate λ 的 estimate，\n      而 λ 本身需要从 empirical data 估计——使得 \"theoretical prediction\" 变成 \n      \"empirical curve fitting with theoretical motivation\"，\n      reviewer 会指出 circular reasoning；\n      (3) 在 14B 上 theory 预测 EDD=2 但实际 EDD=1——这意味着 contraction rate \n      estimation 在 large scale 不准确，可能因为 14B 的 LoRA fine-tune dynamics \n      不满足 theory 的 full fine-tune 假设；\n      (4) 没有 strategy-dependent closed-form 意味着 temp09 reversal 的 \"theoretical explanation\"\n      只是 intuitive argument，不比 empirical observation 本身更有解释力；\n      (5) 净效果：Theory section 对 meta score 仅贡献 +0.1（从 2.8 到 2.9），\n      不足以改变 tier。Reviewer 评价：\n      \"The theoretical sketch provides useful intuition but lacks the rigor \n      expected for a theoretical contribution. The derived bounds do not match \n      empirical results, undermining the claimed theory-experiment connection.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: EDD theoretical bound vs empirical across all tested scales\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"EDD prediction vs actual: scatter plot with error bars showing systematic deviation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section 在 worst 档不救命。它不 address \"no algorithmic contribution\" concern \n      because bound 本身 leaky。Net paper positioning: \n      \"empirical characterization + partial theoretical motivation + honest negative results\"。\n      Simulated reviewer meta-score: 2.8-3.0，accept probability 5-15%。\n      EMNLP Main 在 \"New Missions\" track 可能 borderline accept 如果 framing 够 honest，\n      但需要 2/3 reviewers 对 negative result + characterization value 买账。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Seed robustness (plan_pythia_seed43, plan_olmo_seed43 — RUNNING/ANALYZING)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Seed robustness 3/3 models — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"seed_robustness_aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      Pythia seed43 (ANALYZING) + OLMo seed43 (ANALYZING) + GPT-2 XL seed43 (DONE) \n      的综合 seed robustness 评估。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt2xl_delta_pp: 2.04\n      pythia_delta_pp: 0.64\n      olmo_delta_pp: 2.8\n      max_delta_pp: 2.8\n      mean_delta_pp: 1.83\n      feature_rank_correlation_seed42_vs_43_min: 0.82\n      feature_rank_correlation_seed42_vs_43_mean: 0.90\n      all_seeds_same_edd: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 seed robustness 本身 confirmed (max Δ ≤3pp)，但 reviewer 的问题是 \n      \"so what?\"：\n      (1) GPT-2 XL delta=2.04pp 已 observed，方向一致 (seed43 > seed42)，\n      可能因为 seed43 的 random initialization 恰好 better suited 这个 data split；\n      (2) OLMo delta=2.8pp 是 worst case——接近 3pp upper bound，\n      原因是 OLMo 的 training data (Dolma) 内部 domain diversity 更大，\n      LoRA fine-tune 的 seed sensitivity 与 training data heterogeneity 正相关；\n      (3) Pythia delta=0.64pp 与已观测值 (0.64pp actual) 一致，最 stable——\n      因为 Pile 的 pretraining 使 Pythia 对 fine-tune initialization 更 robust；\n      (4) Feature rank correlation ≥0.82 说明 top features 排序 stable across seeds，\n      但 \"seed stability is minimum requirement not contribution\" in limited scope——\n      reviewer 认为在 ≤1.5B base model + controlled generation 下 seed stability \n      是 expected 而非 surprising；\n      (5) 在 worst tier 叙事下 seed robustness 不能救分——\n      它确认了 \"method works reliably in the narrow regime where it works\"，\n      但 narrow regime 本身是问题。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-seed accuracy delta across 3 models\"\n      - \"Table: Feature importance rank correlation between seeds\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Seed robustness 是 necessary condition 不是 sufficient contribution。\n      在 worst 档下（scope limited to ≤1.5B base），reviewer 认为 seed stability \n      是 minimum bar, 不加分。论文应报告但不 oversell——一句话 \"results are reproducible \n      across random seeds (max Δ=2.8pp)\" 足够，不需要专门 section。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregate: Simulated reviewer + meta-score\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Simulated reviewer meta-assessment — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 worst 档实验结果的模拟 reviewer 评审。\n    expected_results:\n      simulated_reviewer_1_score: 3.0\n      simulated_reviewer_1_comment: >\n        \"The paper provides a thorough characterization of depth signal at small scales,\n        but the 14B failure fundamentally limits the contribution. The theoretical section\n        is suggestive but not rigorous. The comparison with existing detectors shows\n        that much of the signal is already captured by simpler methods at shallow depths.\"\n      simulated_reviewer_2_score: 2.5\n      simulated_reviewer_2_comment: >\n        \"The negative result at 14B is interesting but the paper doesn't adequately explain\n        why. The method's applicability to only ≤1.5B base models is a severe limitation.\n        Seed robustness in this narrow regime is expected, not a contribution.\"\n      simulated_reviewer_3_score: 3.0\n      simulated_reviewer_3_comment: >\n        \"The Atlas and EDD concepts are valuable contributions to the model collapse\n        literature. The honest treatment of scale failure is refreshing. However,\n        the practical impact is limited given the small-model-only scope.\"\n      simulated_meta_score: 2.83\n      accept_probability: 0.10\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档 meta-score 2.83 处于 reject 区间 (EMNLP threshold ~3.5-4.0)：\n      (1) 14B failure + theory mismatch 使得两个原计划的 selling points 失效；\n      (2) Existing detectors 在 shallow depth 的 competitive performance 削弱 novelty；\n      (3) Seed robustness 被视为 minimum requirement 而非 contribution；\n      (4) 唯一获得 positive reception 的是 Atlas/EDD conceptual framework 和 \n      honest negative result treatment；\n      (5) Accept probability 10% 来自 \"New Missions\" track 对 negative results 的 \n      relatively higher tolerance——如果所有 3 reviewers 都认可 \"characterization value\"，\n      可能 borderline accept，但更可能是 \"interesting work, resubmit with stronger \n      theoretical grounding or expanded scale coverage\"。\n      Mitigation path: 如果 EMNLP 被拒，转投 AAAI 2027 或 Findings，\n      在此期间补充 (a) 更多 intermediate scales (3B, 7B-base) 的系统性实验 \n      mapping scale boundary，(b) 改进 theory 使用 actual LM distribution properties \n      而非 Gaussian approximation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档的核心结论：论文变成 \"characterization + negative result\" paper，\n      meta-score ~2.8，accept probability ~10%。\n      可行的 salvage strategy: (a) 将 14B failure 作为 MAIN finding \n      而非 appendix footnote——\"we discovered the scale boundary of depth signal\"；\n      (b) 补充 3B/7B-base 系统性实验 trace boundary 的 exact location；\n      (c) 引用 Shumailov web crawl 数据 argue 1-7B models 仍 contribute \n      disproportionate synthetic text to training corpora；\n      (d) 投 Findings track 作为 backup (acceptance bar lower, ~3.0 sufficient)。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54819,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54819},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22d425ba-df67-4114-a20d-4f05b34d1779","uuid":"a5962039-4803-4910-92f0-58c776a52357"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":209500,"duration_api_ms":211633,"num_turns":1,"result":"我先检查当前 experiment_plan 中所有 status 为 planned 或 RUNNING 的实验，以及 what_if 条目，然后逐一在 worst 档下展开预测。\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe: 从 \"scale-robust depth estimation framework\" 转向 \"characterizing the scale boundary of recursive depth signals\"。\n  14B 实验彻底失败（4-class acc <55%，feature pattern 与 1B 矛盾），theory section 无法解释 scale failure，\n  existing detectors 在 shallow depth 与我们性能接近。论文仍冲 EMNLP Main，但从 framework paper 变为\n  characterization + negative result paper。新 story spine: depth signal 在 ≤1.5B 强且系统性，\n  但在 14B 戏剧性衰减——scale boundary 本身是 finding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: 13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"14B clean FP16 scale validation — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA, nucleus p=0.95, d0-d3 递归链, 19 特征提取, RF/LR 分类。\n      验证 depth signal 在 14B 是否持续。\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.42\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.405, 0.435]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.38\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.37\n      auc_d0v1: 0.78\n      auc_d1v2: 0.53\n      auc_d1v3: 0.62\n      auc_d2v3: 0.52\n      edd_at_075: 1\n      top_features:\n        - p25_ppl\n        - type_token_ratio\n        - mean_ppl\n        - rep_3gram\n        - surprisal_std\n      top2_feature_overlap_with_1b: 0\n      finetune_losses:\n        depth_0: 1.85\n        depth_1: 1.72\n        depth_2: 1.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B 模型容量远大于训练数据复杂度，LoRA fine-tune 后模型快速逼近 attractor distribution，\n      depth-1 与 depth-2/3 的输出分布差异被大模型的 capacity headroom 吸收。具体机制：\n      (1) 14B 的 residual stream 维度（5120 vs 1B 的 2048）使得 LoRA rank-16 的参数扰动\n      相对于总参数量极小（<0.02%），fine-tune 后模型行为变化微弱，递归链各 depth 输出高度相似；\n      (2) finetune loss 从 d0=1.85 到 d2=1.68 仅下降 0.17（1B 模型下降 >1.0），说明\n      14B 在 depth-0 已经 well-fit 数据，后续 depth fine-tune 几乎无额外压缩——\n      Shumailov tail erosion 发生在 depth-0→1 就已完成；\n      (3) d0v1 AUC=0.78 尚可但远低于 1B 的 0.99+，说明即便 real vs gen-1 的区分也大幅退化；\n      (4) top features 完全改变——1B 中 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 是 dominant pair，\n      14B 中这两个特征的跨 depth 方差坍缩，排名退出 top-5，取而代之的是 lexical diversity\n      和低分位 perplexity 特征，这些在 1B 中 importance <0.03；\n      (5) EDD=1（仅 d0v1 AUC>0.75），与 1B 的 EDD=4 严重不一致——\"scale robustness\" claim 不可维持。\n      总结：14B 的 depth signal collapse 是 genuine phenomenon，不是方法缺陷，\n      因为 finetune loss pattern 本身就显示 distribution 在 14B scale 没有足够分化。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 14B vs 1-1.5B comparison — 4-class acc, EDD, top-2 feature overlap\"\n      - \"Table: 14B pairwise AUC matrix (d0v1 through d2v3)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve: 14B (flat near 0.5 for d1v2/d2v3) vs 1B models (monotonic decay from ~0.95)\"\n      - \"Feature importance bar chart: 14B top-10 vs 1B consensus top-10, showing zero overlap in top-2\"\n    analysis: >\n      14B 4-class acc=42% 仅略高于 chance (25%)，且 feature pattern 与 1B 完全矛盾。\n      这构成 worst tier 核心假设的直接确认。论文必须 reframe：depth signal 存在 scale boundary，\n      1-1.5B 内信号强且一致，14B 处信号坍缩。Finetune loss 的 shallow gradient \n      (1.85→1.68 across 3 depths) 提供了机制解释：大模型一次 fine-tune 就到达 attractor 附近，\n      后续 depth 无法产生可区分的 distributional shift。这与 Dohmatob 的 contraction rate 理论\n      一致（capacity 越大，contraction 越快），但 Theory section 的定量 bound 与实际 EDD 不匹配。\n      与 Instruct 实验 (47.4%) 和 base 7B (60%) 共同构成一致 pattern：方法仅对 ≤1.5B base 模型\n      fully effective。必须在 paper 中将此作为 \"scale boundary characterization\" finding，\n      而非 failure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: Wild-data calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      从 C4/FineWeb/RedPajama 抽取子集，用 trained RF 分类器做 depth 预测 + 分布分析，\n      验证 depth signal 在野生数据中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      c4_d0_pct: 62.0\n      c4_fpr: 38.0\n      fineweb_d0_pct: 68.0\n      fineweb_fpr: 32.0\n      redpajama_d0_pct: 60.0\n      redpajama_fpr: 40.0\n      cross_model_consistency_jaccard: 0.35\n      wikitext_d0_pct: 95.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下，wild-data FPR 高达 30-40%，远超此前单数据集实验 (C4 20%, FineWeb 19%)。\n      原因：(1) RedPajama 包含大量 Common Crawl 低质量文本（ads, boilerplate, auto-generated content），\n      这些文本的 repetition + low diversity 特征与 depth-1+ 递归文本高度重叠——\n      RF 的 decision boundary 无法区分 \"genuinely recursive\" 与 \"naturally repetitive\"；\n      (2) 多数据集扩展暴露了之前 OpenWebText (FPR 0.9-2.8%) 是 best case 的事实——\n      editorial-quality web data 很少，raw crawl 的 FPR 才是 realistic deployment scenario；\n      (3) cross-model consistency Jaccard=0.35 远低于此前 controlled 实验的 0.667，\n      说明不同 reference model 对 wild data 的 depth assignment 不一致——\n      在 controlled 设置中 reference model 差异被共享的递归 pattern 掩盖，\n      wild data 中 domain shift 放大了 reference model 偏差；\n      (4) WikiText 仍有 5% FPR（此前 0-1.5%），因为 RedPajama-calibrated RF \n      的 decision boundary shift 导致部分 formulaic academic writing 被误判。\n      结论：depth estimator 在 wild data 的 false positive rate 太高，\n      实际部署需要 domain-specific calibration，这严重限制了 practical claim。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: FPR comparison across 5 datasets (WikiText/C4/FineWeb/OpenWebText/RedPajama)\"\n      - \"Table: Cross-model consistency (3 reference models × 3 datasets)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: FPR by dataset, showing editorial (low) vs crawl (high) pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      FPR 30-40% on raw crawl 意味着 depth estimator 不能 out-of-the-box 部署到 web-scale curation。\n      但 consistent pattern (editorial低/crawl高) 本身是有价值的 finding，\n      说明 FPR 可预测且与 content quality 相关。Paper 必须 honest scope：\n      depth estimation 对 curated corpora 可靠，对 raw crawl 需要额外 domain calibration。\n      这与 worst tier 叙事一致：方法有 clear boundary conditions。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: Existing detector ordinal baseline\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Existing detector ordinal baseline — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT 连续分数校准为 ordinal bin，在 3×3 已有数据上评估\n      ordinal depth estimation 能力。\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc: 0.58\n      binoculars_3class_acc: 0.52\n      binoculars_d0v1_auc: 0.98\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.62\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc: 0.62\n      fastdetectgpt_3class_acc: 0.55\n      fastdetectgpt_d0v1_auc: 0.97\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.68\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.58\n      rf_4class_acc_ref: 0.78\n      delta_rf_vs_best_detector: 0.16\n      detector_shallow_acc_d0d1d2: 0.65\n      rf_shallow_acc_d0d1d2: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档假设 existing detectors 达到 50-65% ordinal acc，这里 Binoculars=58%, \n      Fast-DetectGPT=62%。关键在 shallow depth 的竞争：\n      (1) 两个 detector 在 d0v1 AUC ≈0.97-0.98，与我们的 0.99 几乎相同——\n      real vs gen-1 区分上 existing detectors 本身就足够好，\n      因为它们本来就是为 binary detection 设计的；\n      (2) d1v2 AUC 达到 0.62-0.68，与我们在 topk50 cell 的性能 (0.75-0.83) 有差距\n      但不是 dramatic——特别是 Fast-DetectGPT 的 0.68 与 Pythia topk50 的 0.75 只差 7pp；\n      (3) d2v3 是我们真正拉开差距的地方 (0.55-0.58 vs 我们的 0.69-0.88)，\n      但 reviewer 会指出 deep depth 区分在 practical curation 中 marginal value 有限；\n      (4) 特别危险的是：如果 reviewer 做 binary \"shallow(d0-d1) vs deep(d2-d3)\" simplification，\n      detectors 的表现会更接近我们——因为 coarser granularity 下 existing scores 足够。\n      本质原因：Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT 的 scoring function 隐含 captures depth-related\n      distributional shift 的某些方面（尤其是 tail behavior），虽然不是 ordinal-aware 的，\n      但 calibrated regression 可以利用 score 的 monotonic trend。\n      我们的优势集中在 (a) ordinal structure awareness, (b) d2+ depth pairs，\n      但如果这些 depth 在 14B 消失了，优势领域的 practical relevance 受质疑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: RF vs Binoculars vs Fast-DetectGPT — per-pair AUC comparison\"\n      - \"Table: Simplified binary (shallow/deep) accuracy comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: pairwise AUC by method, showing convergence at shallow depths and divergence at deep\"\n    analysis: >\n      Existing detectors 在 ordinal task 上表现好于 expected (尤其 Fast-DetectGPT 62%)，\n      在 shallow depth (d0/d1) 与 RF 性能接近。我们的 clear advantage 仅在 d2v3 pair。\n      这不致命——我们仍有 16pp advantage overall，且 ordinal structure 是 novel contribution——\n      但 reviewer 可能认为 marginal improvement 不 justify task formalization overhead。\n      Paper 必须强调：(a) detector 的 ordinal acc 是 post-hoc calibration 非 native 能力，\n      (b) 我们提供 interpretable feature analysis (Atlas) 而非 black-box score，\n      (c) cross-strategy robustness 是 detectors 未被测试的。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Table 1 bootstrap CIs\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Table 1 bootstrap CIs — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      从已有 5-fold CV 结果计算 bootstrap confidence intervals for all 9 cells。\n      纯分析任务。\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_pp: 3.2\n      max_ci_width_pp: 5.1\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.671, 0.722]\n      pythia_topk50_ci_width: 5.1\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.838, 0.872]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci_width: 3.4\n      cells_with_ci_width_gt_4pp: 3\n      overlap_between_worst_and_best_cell: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI 宽度取决于 fold variance。Worst 档下，部分 cells（尤其 topk50 cells）\n      的 fold-to-fold variance 较大，导致 CI 宽度达 5pp+。\n      (1) Pythia topk50 是 worst cell (69.6%)，其 fold variance 本身就高（5-fold range ~4pp），\n      bootstrap 放大后 CI 可达 [0.671, 0.722]——下限接近 chance×2.7，不够 impressive；\n      (2) 更关键的是 CI overlap：如果 pythia_topk50 上限 (72.2%) 与 chance baseline \n      的 bootstrap 上限 (28-30%) 还有 gap 没问题，但与 LR baseline (68.2%) 的 CI 重叠——\n      说明在 weakest cell 中 RF vs LR 优势不 statistically significant；\n      (3) 三个 topk50 cells 的 CI width 都 >4pp，说明 topk50 strategy 下 \n      depth signal 本身 noisy，不只是分类器问题；\n      (4) 好消息是 best cells (GPT-2 XL temp09/nucleus) CI tight (3.4pp)，\n      但 reviewer 会 focus on worst cells。\n      本质原因：topk50 的 k=50 truncation 保留了足够 token diversity 使 depth signal 弱于 \n      nucleus (尾部截断更激进→更 distinctive) 和 temp09 (全 logit 放缩→更 distinctive)。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1 (revised): 3×3 matrix with bootstrap 95% CIs\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CI 本身不改变 point estimates，但 worst 档的风险在于 reviewer 关注 CI overlap。\n      如果 weakest cells 的 RF vs simple baseline CI 重叠，\n      reviewer 可能降低对 \"consistent feature-based advantage\" claim 的信心。\n      Mitigation: report CI transparently，强调 9/9 cells 均 >chance (25%) 的 consistency，\n      而非 individual cell significance。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Theoretical analysis (Theory section)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Theoretical analysis — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      连接 depth signal 到 model collapse theory: (1) tail erosion 机制解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal，\n      (2) EDD 上界推导基于 contraction rate，(3) 与实验 EDD 对照验证。\n    expected_results:\n      theory_edd_upper_bound: 3\n      empirical_edd_1b: 4\n      theory_vs_empirical_error: 1\n      theory_edd_bound_14b: 2\n      empirical_edd_14b: 1\n      theory_vs_empirical_error_14b: 1\n      contraction_rate_bound_tight: false\n      tail_erosion_qualitative_match: true\n      tail_erosion_quantitative_match: false\n      strategy_convergence_rate_explanation: \"qualitative only, no closed-form\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 Theory section 的核心问题：无法定量解释 14B failure。\n      (1) Tail erosion 机制（Shumailov et al.）在 1B scale 定性匹配——\n      p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 作为 tail statistics 确实随 depth 单调衰减，\n      与 \"recursive generation erodes tail of learned distribution\" 一致——\n      但定量上，Shumailov 的 Gaussian approximation 预测 tail 衰减速率 \n      与实际 perplexity distribution (heavy-tailed, non-Gaussian) 不匹配：\n      predicted variance contraction ~0.7x per depth vs actual ~0.85x；\n      (2) EDD 上界推导依赖 Dohmatob 的 contraction rate theorem，\n      但该 theorem 假设 distribution family closure (Gaussian → Gaussian)，\n      而实际 LM output distribution 非 Gaussian——推导的 EDD bound=3 < empirical EDD=4，\n      bound 不 tight 且方向错（应是 upper bound，结果低于实际）；\n      (3) 对 14B，理论预测 EDD=2（更快 contraction due to larger capacity），\n      但实际 EDD=1——差距虽然 \"方向一致\" 但具体数值不匹配，\n      且 Theory 无法解释为什么 14B 的 feature pattern 与 1B 完全不同\n      （理论只预测 \"signal weaker\"，不预测 \"feature ranking changes\"）；\n      (4) Strategy-dependent convergence rate（temp09 reversal）只能做 qualitative argument\n      （\"uniform scaling accelerates convergence\"），无 closed-form expression，\n      reviewer 会认为这是 hand-waving；\n      (5) 最致命的是 14B failure + theory mismatch 的组合：\n      如果 theory 能精确预测 \"14B should fail\"，那 negative result 有 explanatory value；\n      但 theory 预测 EDD=2 而实际 EDD=1，说明 theory 连 negative result 也没完全解释。\n      结论：Theory section 从 \"grounding contribution\" 降级为 \"suggestive framework with acknowledged gaps\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Theoretical EDD bound vs empirical EDD across scales (1B, 7B, 14B)\"\n      - \"Table: Predicted vs actual contraction rates by model scale\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contraction rate curve: theoretical prediction vs empirical measurement, showing gap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section 在 worst 档不能作为 independent contribution，\n      只能作为 \"partial explanation\" 放在 Discussion。\n      理论与实验的不一致（EDD bound error ≥1 across scales）\n      使得 \"theoretical grounding\" 这条 sell point 基本失效。\n      Reviewer 可能评论 \"the theoretical analysis is hand-wavy and does not add to the empirical findings\"。\n      Mitigation: 诚实报告 theory 的 limitations，将 theory-empirical gap 本身作为 future work。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_026: API model recursive chains\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"API model recursive chains — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归链 + prompted recursive chain，\n      验证 depth signal 在商用模型中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4omini_ft_4class_acc: 0.38\n      gpt4omini_ft_d1v2_auc: 0.52\n      gpt4omini_prompted_4class_acc: 0.30\n      gpt4omini_prompted_d1v2_auc: 0.51\n      api_cost_usd: 120\n      feature_overlap_with_1b: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 API 模型结果与 14B failure 一致且更极端。\n      (1) GPT-4o-mini 是 distilled large model，其 capacity 远超 1.5B——\n      与 14B 相同的 mechanism (capacity headroom 吸收 recursive perturbation) 适用，\n      且更严重因为 RLHF/DPO alignment 进一步 regularize output distribution，\n      使得不同 depth 的输出更加 homogeneous；\n      (2) Fine-tuning API 限制 (3 epochs max, no LoRA control, black-box optimizer) \n      意味着 fine-tune 幅度可能不足以产生 measurable distributional shift——\n      API model 的 safety guardrails 可能 cap 了 distribution drift；\n      (3) Prompted chain (rewrite/continue without fine-tune) 更糟——\n      大模型的 instruction following 能力使其 \"rewrite\" 时保持 style consistency，\n      depth-1 rewrite 与 depth-0 original 在 statistical features 上几乎不可区分；\n      (4) Feature ranking 完全改变，因为 API model 的 tokenizer 和 vocabulary 不同，\n      且 reference model (Pythia) 与 target model (GPT-4o-mini) 的 distribution mismatch\n      可能主导 feature values，掩盖 genuine depth signal；\n      (5) $120 cost for negative result 是 acceptable 但 reviewer 可能问 \n      \"why not test more API models\" —— 在 worst 档下 one negative 就够了。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: API model depth estimation vs local model comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      API model failure 在 worst 档下是 expected，与 14B failure + instruct failure (47.4%)\n      构成完整 pattern：depth signal 仅在 small base models 中存在。\n      这强化了 \"scale boundary\" 叙事但进一步 narrow 了方法 applicability。\n      Paper 可以 frame 为：\"depth estimation is a small-model phenomenon, \n      which is still practically relevant because small models generate \n      a disproportionate share of recursive web content\"——但这个 argument 的 reviewer \n      acceptability 取决于是否能找到 convincing citation for small model prevalence in web crawl。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # what_if: theory_section\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Theory section (what_if) — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: >\n      Half-page theoretical sketch: tail erosion mechanism, EDD upper bound,\n      strategy convergence rate. 验证与实验数据 consistency。\n    expected_results:\n      tail_erosion_qualitative_fit: true\n      tail_erosion_quantitative_fit: false\n      edd_bound_derivation: \"EDD ≤ floor(log(1/ε) / log(1/λ)) where λ is contraction rate\"\n      edd_bound_1b_predicted: 3\n      edd_bound_1b_actual: 4\n      edd_bound_14b_predicted: 2\n      edd_bound_14b_actual: 1\n      bound_direction: \"consistently underestimates empirical EDD at 1B, overestimates at 14B\"\n      strategy_convergence_closed_form: false\n      reviewer_assessment: \"interesting but not rigorous enough for a theory contribution\"\n      simulated_meta_score_impact: +0.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 plan_023 预测一致。Theory section 的 worst 档特征是 \"directionally correct, \n      quantitatively wrong\"：\n      (1) Tail erosion 定性正确——recursive generation 确实 erodes distribution tails，\n      这与 p90_ppl 的 diagnostic power 一致——但 Shumailov 的 formalism \n      假设 continuous density estimation，而 LM 是 discrete token-level distribution，\n      mapping 不 exact；\n      (2) EDD bound formula 看起来 elegant 但依赖 contraction rate λ 的 estimate，\n      而 λ 本身需要从 empirical data 估计——使得 \"theoretical prediction\" 变成 \n      \"empirical curve fitting with theoretical motivation\"，\n      reviewer 会指出 circular reasoning；\n      (3) 在 14B 上 theory 预测 EDD=2 但实际 EDD=1——这意味着 contraction rate \n      estimation 在 large scale 不准确，可能因为 14B 的 LoRA fine-tune dynamics \n      不满足 theory 的 full fine-tune 假设；\n      (4) 没有 strategy-dependent closed-form 意味着 temp09 reversal 的 \"theoretical explanation\"\n      只是 intuitive argument，不比 empirical observation 本身更有解释力；\n      (5) 净效果：Theory section 对 meta score 仅贡献 +0.1（从 2.8 到 2.9），\n      不足以改变 tier。Reviewer 评价：\n      \"The theoretical sketch provides useful intuition but lacks the rigor \n      expected for a theoretical contribution. The derived bounds do not match \n      empirical results, undermining the claimed theory-experiment connection.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: EDD theoretical bound vs empirical across all tested scales\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"EDD prediction vs actual: scatter plot with error bars showing systematic deviation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Theory section 在 worst 档不救命。它不 address \"no algorithmic contribution\" concern \n      because bound 本身 leaky。Net paper positioning: \n      \"empirical characterization + partial theoretical motivation + honest negative results\"。\n      Simulated reviewer meta-score: 2.8-3.0，accept probability 5-15%。\n      EMNLP Main 在 \"New Missions\" track 可能 borderline accept 如果 framing 够 honest，\n      但需要 2/3 reviewers 对 negative result + characterization value 买账。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Seed robustness (plan_pythia_seed43, plan_olmo_seed43 — RUNNING/ANALYZING)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Seed robustness 3/3 models — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"seed_robustness_aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      Pythia seed43 (ANALYZING) + OLMo seed43 (ANALYZING) + GPT-2 XL seed43 (DONE) \n      的综合 seed robustness 评估。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt2xl_delta_pp: 2.04\n      pythia_delta_pp: 0.64\n      olmo_delta_pp: 2.8\n      max_delta_pp: 2.8\n      mean_delta_pp: 1.83\n      feature_rank_correlation_seed42_vs_43_min: 0.82\n      feature_rank_correlation_seed42_vs_43_mean: 0.90\n      all_seeds_same_edd: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 seed robustness 本身 confirmed (max Δ ≤3pp)，但 reviewer 的问题是 \n      \"so what?\"：\n      (1) GPT-2 XL delta=2.04pp 已 observed，方向一致 (seed43 > seed42)，\n      可能因为 seed43 的 random initialization 恰好 better suited 这个 data split；\n      (2) OLMo delta=2.8pp 是 worst case——接近 3pp upper bound，\n      原因是 OLMo 的 training data (Dolma) 内部 domain diversity 更大，\n      LoRA fine-tune 的 seed sensitivity 与 training data heterogeneity 正相关；\n      (3) Pythia delta=0.64pp 与已观测值 (0.64pp actual) 一致，最 stable——\n      因为 Pile 的 pretraining 使 Pythia 对 fine-tune initialization 更 robust；\n      (4) Feature rank correlation ≥0.82 说明 top features 排序 stable across seeds，\n      但 \"seed stability is minimum requirement not contribution\" in limited scope——\n      reviewer 认为在 ≤1.5B base model + controlled generation 下 seed stability \n      是 expected 而非 surprising；\n      (5) 在 worst tier 叙事下 seed robustness 不能救分——\n      它确认了 \"method works reliably in the narrow regime where it works\"，\n      但 narrow regime 本身是问题。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-seed accuracy delta across 3 models\"\n      - \"Table: Feature importance rank correlation between seeds\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Seed robustness 是 necessary condition 不是 sufficient contribution。\n      在 worst 档下（scope limited to ≤1.5B base），reviewer 认为 seed stability \n      是 minimum bar, 不加分。论文应报告但不 oversell——一句话 \"results are reproducible \n      across random seeds (max Δ=2.8pp)\" 足够，不需要专门 section。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregate: Simulated reviewer + meta-score\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Simulated reviewer meta-assessment — worst\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 worst 档实验结果的模拟 reviewer 评审。\n    expected_results:\n      simulated_reviewer_1_score: 3.0\n      simulated_reviewer_1_comment: >\n        \"The paper provides a thorough characterization of depth signal at small scales,\n        but the 14B failure fundamentally limits the contribution. The theoretical section\n        is suggestive but not rigorous. The comparison with existing detectors shows\n        that much of the signal is already captured by simpler methods at shallow depths.\"\n      simulated_reviewer_2_score: 2.5\n      simulated_reviewer_2_comment: >\n        \"The negative result at 14B is interesting but the paper doesn't adequately explain\n        why. The method's applicability to only ≤1.5B base models is a severe limitation.\n        Seed robustness in this narrow regime is expected, not a contribution.\"\n      simulated_reviewer_3_score: 3.0\n      simulated_reviewer_3_comment: >\n        \"The Atlas and EDD concepts are valuable contributions to the model collapse\n        literature. The honest treatment of scale failure is refreshing. However,\n        the practical impact is limited given the small-model-only scope.\"\n      simulated_meta_score: 2.83\n      accept_probability: 0.10\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档 meta-score 2.83 处于 reject 区间 (EMNLP threshold ~3.5-4.0)：\n      (1) 14B failure + theory mismatch 使得两个原计划的 selling points 失效；\n      (2) Existing detectors 在 shallow depth 的 competitive performance 削弱 novelty；\n      (3) Seed robustness 被视为 minimum requirement 而非 contribution；\n      (4) 唯一获得 positive reception 的是 Atlas/EDD conceptual framework 和 \n      honest negative result treatment；\n      (5) Accept probability 10% 来自 \"New Missions\" track 对 negative results 的 \n      relatively higher tolerance——如果所有 3 reviewers 都认可 \"characterization value\"，\n      可能 borderline accept，但更可能是 \"interesting work, resubmit with stronger \n      theoretical grounding or expanded scale coverage\"。\n      Mitigation path: 如果 EMNLP 被拒，转投 AAAI 2027 或 Findings，\n      在此期间补充 (a) 更多 intermediate scales (3B, 7B-base) 的系统性实验 \n      mapping scale boundary，(b) 改进 theory 使用 actual LM distribution properties \n      而非 Gaussian approximation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档的核心结论：论文变成 \"characterization + negative result\" paper，\n      meta-score ~2.8，accept probability ~10%。\n      可行的 salvage strategy: (a) 将 14B failure 作为 MAIN finding \n      而非 appendix footnote——\"we discovered the scale boundary of depth signal\"；\n      (b) 补充 3B/7B-base 系统性实验 trace boundary 的 exact location；\n      (c) 引用 Shumailov web crawl 数据 argue 1-7B models 仍 contribute \n      disproportionate synthetic text to training corpora；\n      (d) 投 Findings track 作为 backup (acceptance bar lower, ~3.0 sufficient)。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"22d425ba-df67-4114-a20d-4f05b34d1779","total_cost_usd":0.63417225,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54819,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":9431,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9431,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":49778,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.049848,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9431,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54819,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.58432425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2370f669-e623-4a85-87e6-2ea0578ca7c4"}
